sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch04-17> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch04-17--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch04-17--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch04-17: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.49" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.489"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.56"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Geological rates are estimable from the fossil record, and generation-scale experiments show that selection need not be slow on an ecological clock. Which clock the wording uses is ambiguous, so the same data can be read as compatible or as a counterexample. Selection gradients for whole regional biotas are not in one open dataset, which limits the test to proxies and well-studied cases." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Measure rates of phenotypic and genomic change per generation and per geological interval, and the fraction of co-occurring species showing concurrent directional change. The claim would be confirmed if change is almost always geologically slow, intermittent, and limited to a small minority of species in a region; rapid, simultaneous responses in many co-occurring species would refute the strong reading. The word slowly still needs a declared timescale." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Slowly can mean per-generation selection or the geological appearance of new forms, and those are different tests.", "Field estimates of selection differentials are scattered across studies.", "Abundance change in monitoring series is not the same variable as selection." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch04-17--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch04-17--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch04-17--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch04-17--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch04-17 by Grok 4.7: 0.5" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.5"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch04-17--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch04-17> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch04-17--grok--operationalizability> .
